  "2. Shelf correction: the adjacent <basename>.correction.json must be byte-identical at shelf.commit and at the current HEAD of the shelf repository, else REJECTED (STALE_CORRECTION; re-admit the entry at the HEAD). A correction that is present must name these exact bytes (repository, path, sha256), else REJECTED. When it sets supersedes_historical_status_for_admission, its qualification_claim is the effective verdict. Signed bundles admit no correction file (CORRECTION_UNSUPPORTED).",
  "3. Signed bundles: key from the source commit's first-parent .aien/verify.pub, Ed25519 signature, repository, commit, executor, required gates from .aien/always and verdict algebra must all hold, else REJECTED; the effective verdict is the bundle verdict.",
  "4. Omega receipts without a superseding correction: the named source commit must resolve upstream and every recoverable source artifact must hash to the recorded digest; otherwise the effective verdict is REFUSED_SOURCE_PROVENANCE. build/ outputs are never recoverable and are not counted.",
  "5. Replay recomputes every field except id and replay, and replay must read `python3 tools/replay_receipt.py replay <id>`. issue_or_gate is derived from the receipt (bundle repository and required gates; Omega milestone and contract_id); a receipt that names none carries operator text marked verified false, and replay prints it as UNVERIFIED. Any difference from this file is REJECTED (INDEX_DRIFT); an index or entry field this tool does not know is REJECTED (UNKNOWN_FIELD)."
